================================================================================
Third-party material
================================================================================

Oscilla's probe firmware studies two upstream MIT-licensed projects. No source
from either project is copied into the current 802.15.4 implementation. Both
remain under their original licenses and copyrights; nothing here relicenses
them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C5Lab projectZero
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License: MIT

Referenced by Oscilla as follows (DESIGN.md §11):

  * Studied and reimplemented clean-room
      - zig_recon/ behavior and protocol boundaries (IEEE 802.15.4 PAN and
        node discovery)
        Oscilla's implementation lives in firmware-c5/main/zig_*.c and copies
        no projectZero source.

  * Referenced and reimplemented (no code copied)
      - the D-UCB discounted-bandit channel picker
      - promiscuous-mode channel hopping
      - NimBLE scan parameters
      - Wi-Fi band-mode handling
        Location: firmware-c5/main/

  * Deliberately not used
      - the main.c monolith
      - frame_analyzer, sniffer, pcap_serializer, hccapx_serializer
        (deferred: the Oscilla probe has no SD card, so these would require
        streaming frames over the control link — see docs/DECISIONS.md D-2)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
esp32-wifi-penetration-tool — Martin Risinek (@risinek)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License: MIT

The upstream project from which projectZero descends. Oscilla studied its
architecture and its ESP32 Wi-Fi recon patterns. Original copyright and
@risinek attribution headers are preserved in any file that carries them.

Note on scope: that project includes active/offensive capabilities. Oscilla
takes none of them. Oscilla v1 is receive-only on every radio — no transmit
verb is compiled into any build, so there is no reachable firmware code path
to transmission (DESIGN.md §8, docs/DECISIONS.md D-8).

